From d4b50f3c8254a3eefa091b8a111a779fc2ed314c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Broyojo <dha@xoba.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:01:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Present with display sync when the game asks for vsync,
 as Windows does

mtld3d always turned Metal-side vsync off (displaySyncEnabled = false) and
mapped a vsync request to a present throttle only, so every game could
tear. Follow Windows instead. A fullscreen device follows its
presentation interval: any interval but IMMEDIATE waits for a display
refresh and never tears, IMMEDIATE presents at once. A windowed device
always waits for a refresh, as DWM composites windowed presents whatever
their interval (Source ignores its own vsync setting in a window for that
reason). The layer's display sync is set at attach and follows a Reset
that changes the request.

A new present.vsync key (game, on, off; default game) overrides the game
for titles that offer no vsync setting of their own. The throttle stays
for present.maxFps and divided intervals.
